Donald Trump's big beautiful wall his  supporters love the idea the primetime  address was the deal maker in chief's  last-ditch effort to sell it to  skeptical Americans at the request of  Democrats it will be a steel barrier  rather than a concrete wall this barrier  is absolutely critical to border  security it's also what our  professionals at the border want indeed  this is just common sense the border  wall would very quickly pay for itself  the cost of illegal drugs exceeds 500  billion dollars a year vastly more than  the 5.7 billion dollars we have  requested from Congress the wall will  also be paid for indirectly by the great  new trade deal we have made with Mexico  poised fact-checkers were quick to point  out that the Democrats did not request a  steel barrier along the border nor would  that new trade deal have any direct  impact on funding for a wall but Trump  isn't one to let facts get in the way of  a good sales pitch once again he painted  those crossing the border as criminals  highlighting brutal crimes committed by  illegal immigrants while statistics show  that crime rate among immigrants is  actually lower than among US citizens  Trump is so obviously more comfortable  at a campaign rally than he is in the  stuffy confines of the Oval Office where  he tried out a softer approach aiming  directly for the heart for those who  refuse to compromise in the name of  border security  I would ask imagine if it was your child  your husband or your wife whose life was  so cruelly shattered and totally broken  to every member of Congress pass a bill  that ends this crisis Democratic leaders  have so far shown zero sign of giving  Trump what he wants to end the  government shutdown and there was no  indication of that changing in there  our own address to the nation sadly much  of what we heard from president Trump  throughout this sense of shutdown has  been full of misinformation and even  malice most presidents have used Oval  Office addresses for noble purposes this  president just used the backdrop of the  Oval Office to manufacture a crisis  stoke fear and divert attention from the  turmoil in his administration  we need border security rather flat  televised addresses contrasted the  heated oval office meeting between Trump  and the Democrats one month ago it's  also a reminder of how little has  changed during that time each side seems  only more entrenched in their own  position talk of Trump exercising  emergency powers did not materialize but  that doesn't mean it's off the cards  right now compromise feels like the  least likely outcome halfway through  week three of the shutdown it's becoming  increasingly hard to see a way forward  Amanda Walker's Sky News Washington
 

